
# DocConnect

DocConnect is a healthcare professional networking app. It has two screens: Home and Discover.

The Home page shows the doctor profile and posts. The Discover page shows people who can be connected with.

## Technologies Used

- React Native
- Expo
- Node.js
- Express.js
- MongoDB
- Mongoose

## Project Structure

```text
DocConnect/
├── app/
│   ├── index.tsx
│   └── discover.tsx
├── assets/
├── backend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── models/
│   │   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── server.js
│   │   └── seed.js
│   └── .env
└── README.md
```

## Requirements

Before running the project, install these:

- Node.js
- MongoDB Community Server
- Expo Go or an Android emulator

## MongoDB Setup

First, install MongoDB Community Server and make sure the MongoDB service is running.

The project uses a database called `docconnect`.

In the backend `.env` file, add:

```env
PORT=5000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/docconnect
```

MongoDB will create the database when the application first inserts data.

## Run the Backend

Open a terminal and go to the backend folder:

```bash
cd backend
```

Install the packages:

```bash
npm install
```

Start the backend server:

```bash
npm run start
```

If everything works, the terminal should show:

```text
MongoDB Connected
Server running on port 5000
```

## Add Sample Data

Before using the app, run the seed script to add sample users and posts to MongoDB.

Open another terminal in the backend folder and run:

```bash
node src/seed.js
```

The script creates sample users and posts for the Home and Discover screens.

It also prints the first user's ID. Copy that ID because it is used as the current user in the frontend.

Note: Running the seed script again deletes and recreates the sample users, posts, and connections.

## Run the App

Open another terminal in the main project folder, where the Expo `package.json` is located.

Install the packages:

```bash
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file in the frontend folder:

```env
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:5000/api
EXPO_PUBLIC_CURRENT_USER_ID=PASTE_FIRST_USER_ID_HERE
```

Replace the ID with the one printed by the seed script.

For an Android emulator, use `10.0.2.2` to access the backend running on your computer.

For a physical phone using Expo Go, replace `10.0.2.2` with your computer's local IP address. Make sure both devices are connected to the same Wi-Fi network.

Start Expo:

```bash
npx expo start
```

Scan the QR code with Expo Go or open the app in your emulator.

## API Routes

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/users` | Get all users |
| GET | `/api/users/:id` | Get one user |
| GET | `/api/posts` | Get all posts |
| GET | `/api/posts/:id` | Get one post |
| GET | `/api/connections/:userId` | Get connection requests |
| POST | `/api/connections` | Send a connection request |
| PATCH | `/api/connections/:id/accept` | Accept a connection request |

## Notes

- Start MongoDB before running the backend.
- Run the seed script before testing with sample data.
- Keep the backend running while using the app.
- The frontend `.env` file and backend `.env` file have different settings.
- The app currently contains the Home and Discover screens.
